Stop the SPA from downloading the repo-info `siblings` list.

`repoAPI.getInfo` is the SPA's only caller of the repo-info endpoint,
and no UI code reads `repoInfo.siblings` (the file tree comes from
`/tree/`). On a 40k-file dataset that list is a 6 MB response that the
SPA waits on in `onMounted` before it loads the README, so the card
feels slow for no benefit. Ask the backend for the metadata-only shape
(see 0002) instead.

Homepage/user pages that embed a README keep working — they fetch the
tree and the README separately.

--- a/src/kohaku-hub-ui/src/utils/api.js
+++ b/src/kohaku-hub-ui/src/utils/api.js
@@ -181,7 +181,9 @@
    * @returns {Promise} - Repository metadata
    */
   getInfo: (type, namespace, name) =>
-    api.get(`/api/${type}s/${namespace}/${name}`),
+    api.get(`/api/${type}s/${namespace}/${name}`, {
+      params: { include_siblings: false },
+    }),
 
   /**
    * List repositories
